    <p class="lede first reveal">Affiliate marketing has a reputation problem, and it earned every bit of it. For years it was the province of people stuffing links into content they didn't believe, chasing pennies on a product they'd never touched. So when someone tells you it's how they make money online, a part of you flinches.</p>
    <p class="reveal">Here is the version that actually works, and it's almost the opposite of the reputation. You recommend the handful of tools you genuinely use — the ones you'd tell a friend about for free — and you earn a small cut when someone buys through your link. That's it. No inventory, no product to build, no customer service.</p>
    <p class="reveal"><strong>The catch isn't that it's hard. It's that it's easy to do badly.</strong> The whole thing runs on one asset — whether people believe you — and that asset is destroyed the first time you recommend something for the commission instead of the reader. Get that one thing right and affiliate income is the lightest money in this business.</p>

