    <div class="chapter reveal"><span class="bignum">01</span><div class="num">Chapter One</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="what">What affiliate marketing actually is — and isn't</h2></div>
    <p class="answer reveal">Affiliate marketing is earning a commission by recommending someone else's product through a tracked link. You don't own the product, hold inventory, or handle the sale — you connect a person to a solution and earn a share when they buy.</p>
    <p class="reveal">What it isn't: a way to get rich by spamming links. The link is the last, smallest part. The real work is the recommendation — being the person whose opinion someone trusts enough to act on. <strong>The link monetises trust you've already built; it cannot manufacture trust you haven't.</strong></p>
    <div class="box tip reveal"><span class="tag"><span class="g">✦</span> The Edit</span><p>Think of yourself as a good friend with taste, not a billboard. A friend says "get this one, skip that one, and here's why." A billboard shouts at everyone. Only one of those gets a click that turns into a sale — and a reader who comes back.</p></div>

    <div class="triptych offset reveal">
