    <div class="chapter left reveal"><span class="bignum">06</span><div class="num">Chapter Six</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="programs">The programs worth starting with</h2></div>
    <p class="answer reveal">The best affiliate programs for a beginner are the ones for tools you already use daily — your design tool, your email platform, your favourite templates — because you can recommend them honestly and repeatedly.</p>
    <p class="reveal">Don't start by hunting for programs. Start by listing the tools you'd recommend anyway, then check which of them have an affiliate program. That order keeps you honest and saves you from building around a payout you don't believe in.</p>

    <div class="detail reveal">
      <div class="photo mask img" style="background-image:url(/images/library/product-ribbon-notecards.jpg);background-size:cover;background-position:center"></div>
      <div class="say"><div class="k">The best programs, in one line</div><p>Tools you'd defend without a commission. Design software, email platforms, and resellable products you've actually put your hands on beat any high-payout program for something you've never opened.</p></div>
    </div>

    <div class="box action reveal"><span class="tag"><span class="g">→</span> Action Step</span><h4>List five, check for programs</h4><p>Write down the five tools you'd recommend even if nobody paid you. Check which have an affiliate program. Those are your starting recommendations — honest by design, because you chose them before you knew the payout.</p><a class="btn dark" href="/learn/digital-products-guide">The Digital Products Guide <span class="a">→</span></a></div>

    <div class="chapter reveal"><span class="bignum">07</span><div class="num">Chapter Seven</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="repeat">Turning one recommendation into income that repeats</h2></div>
    <p class="answer reveal">A single affiliate link becomes repeating income when it lives inside evergreen content — a post or pin that keeps getting found — so the recommendation you wrote once keeps earning as new readers arrive.</p>
    <p class="reveal">The one-off tweet earns once. The well-written comparison article earns for years, because it keeps surfacing in search and answering the same question for new people. That's the shift: from chasing clicks to building an asset that recommends on your behalf while you sleep.</p>

    <div class="spread right reveal">
      <div class="frame" style="background-image:url(/images/library/flatlay-digital-workbook.jpg);background-size:cover;background-position:center"></div>
