    <div class="chapter reveal"><div class="num">Answered</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="faq">Frequently asked</h2></div>
    <h3 class="reveal">How do beginners start affiliate marketing without an audience?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">Write genuinely useful content — a comparison, a how-to, a recommendation — around a question people already search, and place honest affiliate links inside it. Pinterest and blog search bring the readers; you don't need a following, you need to be the answer someone finds.</p>
    <h3 class="reveal">Do I have to pay to join affiliate programs?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">No. Reputable affiliate programs are free to join. If a program asks you to pay to become an affiliate, treat that as a warning sign and walk away.</p>
    <h3 class="reveal">How much can I realistically earn?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">It varies enormously and it starts small. Early affiliate income is often a few sales a month; it compounds as your evergreen content accumulates and keeps getting found. Treat the first commission as proof the model works, not as the ceiling.</p>

